content.text:
The evidence points to one fault, an HTTP abort on travel-plan's outgoing `quickestRoute` calls. The incident is confined to that path, and the other travel-plan → route-plan paths still succeed.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_aborted",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT regexp_extract(message, 'I/O error on (\\w+) request for \"([^\"]+)\"', 2) AS url, regexp_extract(message, '(Connection reset|Unexpected end of file[^;]*)', 1) AS err, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND level='SEVERE' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "About 1,509 travel-plan SEVERE logs show 'Unexpected end of file' on outgoing route-plan quickestRoute calls; 54 more are connection resets."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' AS p, span_name, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND span_name LIKE '%getQuickestRoutes%' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', span_name, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND span_name LIKE '%getQuickestRoutes%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Route-plan's getQuickestRoutes handler produced 48 spans normally but none in the incident, so the requests never arrived."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM (SELECT 'abn' AS p, * FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', * FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND span_name='POST' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY p, attr_status_code",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's outgoing POST client spans fail with Error status in the incident, about 1,565 of them, while normal shows none."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' AS p, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice/travelPlan/quickest' UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', count(*), sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice/travelPlan/quickest'",
          "claim": "UI dashboard's quickest-travel-plan requests error 89 of 108 times in the incident versus 0 of 48 normally."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

